---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/**
 * What a visitor got until now was S3's own AccessDenied XML, with a 403.
 *
 * Two things wrong with that. It said "access denied" about a page that simply
 * does not exist, which invites the reader to think they are being kept out of
 * something. And a 403 tells a search engine the page is forbidden rather than
 * absent, so a mistyped link stayed in an index instead of dropping out of it.
 *
 * The 403 is S3's doing, not a mistake: the bucket is not public and denies a
 * missing key rather than admitting it is missing. The distribution turns both
 * 403 and 404 into this page — see custom_error_response in terraform.
 */
---
<Base title="Not found — mimawsi">
  <h1>Nothing here</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    That page does not exist. It may have been a typo, or a link to a tool that
    was never published — or one that was taken down.
  </p>

  <p class="hint">
    Every tool that is published stays published at the same address, so a link
    that used to work should still work. If one has stopped, that is worth
    knowing about.
  </p>

  <p class="go">
    <a class="cta" href="/">All tools</a>
    <a href="/share">Share a tool</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .hint { opacity: .75; }
  .go {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
